All evidence collected. Here is the verification:

**VERIFICATION OF m008 — Belady 1966 Citation Conflict**

**Sources checked (named):**
- DBLP IBM Systems Journal Vol 5 TOC: `dblp.org/db/journals/ibmsj/ibmsj5.html` — fetched, confirmed
- IEEE Xplore via DOI 10.1147/sj.52.0078 redirect: `ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/5388441/` — fetched, confirmed
- DOI resolver for 10.1147/sj.52.0149: `doi.org` — HTTP 404, confirmed

**Resolution:**

There is ONE Belady 1966 paper in IBM Systems Journal Vol 5 No 2:
- Title: "A Study of Replacement Algorithms for a Virtual-Storage Computer"
- Author: L. A. Belady
- Venue: IBM Systems Journal Vol 5 No 2 (1966)
- Pages: 78-101
- DOI: 10.1147/sj.52.0078

The "pp 149-159" claim is a citation error. DBLP Vol 5 No 2 TOC lists: Freeman pp 62-77, Belady pp 78-101, Spielberg pp 102-114, Chang pp 115-125 — no gap, no second Belady entry. The Bricault/Delgalvis paper "On Teleprocessing System Design Part III" is pp 148-157 but it sits in Vol 5 No 3 (the next issue), not No 2. The space-bunny lane misread the IEEE article-ID suffix "0149" as page 149, then conflated it with the adjacent-issue Bricault pages. DOI 10.1147/sj.52.0149 itself returns HTTP 404 — it does not resolve to any article.

